                <pb facs="0792" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg696"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in Mr. Bingham’s No. 788.—Extract from
                        the Japan Daily Mail, October 10, 1879.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Notification No</hi>. 42.</head>
                <p>It is hereby notified that as ever since the revision of article 318 of the
                    Keitei Ritswiei (amended code) notified by notification No. 86, in June, 1876,
                    torture to extract confession is not to be used; all laws and regulations
                    relating thereto (torture) have all been abrogated.</p>
                <closer><signed>SANJO SANEYOSHI,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Prime
                        Minister.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
